<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John VIII, Count of Nassau-Siegen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1583">1583</a>–<a href="/years/1638">1638</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as John the Younger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John VIII, Count of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegen">Siegen</a>, known as John the Younger, was a son of John VII. He converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> in 1612 and served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> as a general. His Catholic line ruled part of Nassau-Siegen while the Reformed line of his half-brothers held the rest, leaving the town and county divided by confession.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-viii-count-of-nassau-siegen.jpg" alt="John VIII, Count of Nassau-Siegen" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan van Ravesteyn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En_atelier_Jan_Anthonisz_van_Ravesteyn_-_Portrait_of_Jan_III_(1583-1638),_Count_of_Nassau-Siegen_-_418_-_Mauritshuis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
